| `$name` | $line | $status |

@@ line_halts_budget
on every input on which the $build build is never refused memory for exceeding $budget (a premise), it exits with $exits$binds
@@ line_halts_may_fail
with no memory premise, and even if any request is refused at any time: the $build build exits with $exits
@@ line_agreement
on every input on which the plain build is never refused memory for exceeding $budget (a premise): neither build reaches an error and both have the same set of observable behaviours; $fires$variant$own
@@ own_budgets
 (this project's own budgets: $plain / $san)
@@ fires
$san never fires
@@ fires_ubsan_rust
no UB check fails
@@ fires_asan-ubsan_rust
neither ASan nor a UB check fires
@@ line_bound
P[plain and $san disagree] <= b under [Distribution.v](Distribution.v)
@@ line_decidability
some program decides exactly the inputs where plain and $san agree
@@ line_classifier_sound_a_published
classifier $role, when it answers yes, is right that plain and $san agree, and never answers no where they do
@@ line_classifier_sound_a_unpatched
classifier $role, when it answers yes, is right that plain and $san without the patches agree, and never answers no where they do
@@ line_classifier_sound_b_published
classifier $role, when it answers yes, is right that each of plain and $san does the same at every pair of entries, and never answers no where they do
@@ line_classifier_sound_b_unpatched
classifier $role, when it answers yes, is right that each of plain and $san agrees with its build without the patches, and never answers no where they do
@@ line_classifier_total
classifier $role of the plain and $san pair always answers yes, no or maybe
@@ line_classifier_maybe_bound
P[classifier $role of the plain and $san pair gives no firm answer] <= b under [Distribution.v](Distribution.v)
@@ line_classifier_maybe_empty
classifier $role of the plain and $san pair gives every valid input a firm answer
@@ line_classifier_bound
P[classifier $role of the plain and $san pair does not answer yes] <= b under [Distribution.v](Distribution.v)

@@ uninstrumented
Each build also links code that no sanitizer instruments, as its link recorded it. A statement about a sanitizer build covers that code only as uninstrumented code: ASan checks no load or store made inside it, and UBSan inserts no check there.

$rows

@@ uninstrumented_row
- $build: $items
@@ uninstrumented_none
The toolchain's runtimes (the C library, compiler-rt, the sanitizer runtime and the C++ runtime) are not instrumented in any build. Which other code each build links uninstrumented is not recorded in this release.

